 mba  program has more people with high gmat  scores  this can help them to score high in the  gmat and from the perspective of a  candidate if you don't want to apply for  mba programs and you check out all these  gmail scores and you were able to score  high  of course you'd rather want to be in a  class with lots of other people who  scored high in the gmat as well because  the gmat is a good proxy for how well  you will be able to perform in a  business context and it is also  correlated with future career success  this is exactly how the gmat was set up  why people developed the gmat in the  first place so put lots of preparation  into your gmat to score  as high as possible and if you score  high this can really help you to get  into one of the most selective mba  programs and if you're doing one of  these very prestigious mba programs this  can help you significantly in your  career and then also to do all kinds of  career transitions that you might want  to do but do not get me wrong here of  course i'm very well aware that scoring  high on the gmat is not easy and i made  a whole video about how i prepared for  the gmat the tips and tricks and  strategies that i use to score above 700  on my personal gmat exam  if you haven't seen that yet also i have  it included here in a link  above check it out so yes of course it's  not easy it's not easy to get into the  most selective most prestigious on the a  programs of the world but the point that  i just want to stress is that the gmat  can really help you to overcome  many weaknesses of your profile of the  past with a high gmat of course there's  no guarantee to get into all kinds of  mba programs but it will be a big help  so if you're looking to do that  transition do an mba and try to get an  mba that is  as selective as competitive as possible  in terms of the rankings and to get in  there  do a gmat and try to score as high as  possible to get in this is just a little  reflection on the live stream that i did  earlier because there were many people  asking questions in that direction i  hope this is helpful and insightful to  you please if you liked the video  hit the like button for the youtube  algorithm and also subscribe to this  channel for more content on how you can  be successful  in the first years of your career thanks  to all of you for watching this was  heineken from learning goodbye
 

